# C/C++ unit-test function naming (local elaboration)

This is a **local** elaboration of shared **test-standards**. It is not yet in the upstream rulesbase.


## Rule

Unit-test functions (xTests cases and similar) must be named as follows:

* Prefix **`TEST_`** (not `test_`).
* Remaining name parts are **SHOUTING** (`UPPER_SNAKE`), separated by `_`.
* **Exceptions** — keep the conventional spelling (not forced to shouting) when a part is:
  * a **construct name** (API/type/function identifier as used in the product, e.g. `libver_find`, `libver_init`);
  * a **language identifier** or reserved form (e.g. `NULL`, `errno` where that is the subject).


## Examples

```c
/* ✅ required */
static void TEST_libver_init_AND_libver_uninit(void);
static void TEST_libver_find_STUB_RETURNS_NO_SCHEMES(void);
static void TEST_libver_find_NULL_result(void);

/* ❌ forbidden */
static void test_init_uninit(void);
static void test_find_null_result(void);
static void TEST_INIT_UNINIT(void); /* hides the libver_init / libver_uninit constructs */
```


## Scope

Applies to new and edited unit/component test sources under this repository until the rule is folded into upstream **test-standards**.
